\label{rem:ergodic-averaging-diffusion-extension}
The proof of \cref{thm:glauber-recovers-average-gradient,thm:glauber-recovers-average-hessian} is quite flexible and can be changed slightly to yield similar results for a large family of stochastic processes (beyond Glauber Dynamics).
For instance, the Green operator and Dynkin martingale arguments can be adapted to Markov diffusion processes on compact Riemannian manifolds, using pointwise carr\'e du champ estimates obtained via the Bakry--\'Emery curvature-dimension condition~\citep[Section~1.16]{bakry2013analysis}. In our forthcoming companion paper~\citep{das2026averaged} on spherical tensor PCA, we apply these techniques to establish analogous recovery guarantees for spherical Langevin dynamics.

