\label{thm:strong-recovery-after-weak-recovery}
Let $k$ be even, let $(X_t)_{t\geqslant0}$ denote Glauber dynamics for $H$ at inverse temperature $\beta>0$, and fix arbitrary constants $\rho\in(0,1)$ and $\eta\in(0,1)$. Assume $\lambda\geqslant C_{\beta,k,\rho}N^{\tfrac{k-2}{4}}$, where $C_{\beta,k,\rho}$ is a sufficiently large constant, and set $T_{\mathrm{str}}\doteq\log N$. Then, the following holds for all sufficiently large $N$, every deterministic $T$ satisfying $T_{\mathrm{str}}\leqslant T\leqslant\operatorname{poly}(N)$, and any initial state $X_0$ with $\abs{m(X_0)}\geqslant\rho$, possibly depending on $H$,
\begin{align*}
    \mathbb{P}\left[\inf_{t\in[T_{\mathrm{str}},T]}\abs{m(X_t)}\geqslant1-N^{-\eta}\right]
    \geqslant1-\exp(-c_kN)-\exp(-cN^{1-\eta})-NT\exp\left(-k\beta\lambda\left(\frac{\rho}{2}\right)^{k-1}\right).
\end{align*}

Throughout the proof, we assume that $N$ is sufficiently large. Let $X_0$ be any initial state with $\abs{m(X_0)}\geqslant\rho$, possibly depending on $H$, and define
\begin{align*}
    \widetilde x^\star\doteq\operatorname{sgn}\bigl(m(X_0)\bigr)x^{\star},
    \qquad
    \widetilde m(x)\doteq\frac1N\left\langle \widetilde x^\star, x \right\rangle.
\end{align*}
Observe that $\widetilde m(X_0)=\abs{m(X_0)}\geqslant\rho$ and $\abs{m(x)}\geqslant\widetilde m(x)$ for every $x\in\Omega_N$. Moreover, since $k$ is even, $H=N\lambda\widetilde m^k+H_0$. Consider the event
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{E}\doteq\left\{\max_{x\in\Omega_N} 
